# photo2motion.studio (Netlify project "photo2motion", from github.com/Not-Bad-Studio/photo2motion).
# The first rule that matches wins. Pages need no rule: Netlify serves hospitality.html at /hospitality.

# www goes to the bare domain.
https://www.photo2motion.studio/*   https://photo2motion.studio/:splat   301!
http://www.photo2motion.studio/*    https://photo2motion.studio/:splat   301!

# Icons at the root, where browsers and Google's favicon fetcher look first. The pages link the files in /images/brand.
/favicon.ico            /images/brand/p2m-favicon.ico            200!
/apple-touch-icon.png   /images/brand/p2m-apple-touch-icon.png   200!

# Other names the home and sector pages have had (the files were photo2motion.html and p2m-<sector>.html on the
# Not Bad Studio site until the move).
/index.html          /              301!
/photo2motion        /              301!
/photo2motion.html   /              301!
/p2m-hospitality     /hospitality   301!
/p2m-property        /property      301!
/p2m-marine          /marine        301!

# The private client pages, photo2motion.studio/for/<page>/, come from the demos site (Netlify project photo2motion-demos, nbs-motion-demos until 24 Nov 2026,
# built and deployed from ~/Sites/motion-demos). /for on its own has no page, so it goes home. Netlify treats /for and
# /for/ as one path, so /for must never point at /for/ (that looped until 21 Nov 2026).
/for     /                                              301!
/for/*   https://photo2motion-demos.netlify.app/:splat    200!

# Delivered films, photo2motion.studio/get/<token>/, come from the photo2motion-files project (built and deployed by
# motion-demos/tools/deliver.py; its edge function ends each link after 30 days). /get on its own has no page, and
# like /for it must never point at /get/.
/get     /                                                    301!
/get/*   https://photo2motion-files.netlify.app/get/:splat   200!

# Checkout, free clips, the Stripe webhook and the jobs board still run on the Not Bad Studio site, with their keys and
# the Netlify forms that email each order. Forward them there until they move (stage 3 in README.md).
/api/*   https://www.notbadstudio.com/api/:splat        200!
